Z||000005||Nashco||12-09-2001||04:20 AM||||You guys must have missed that part that says it is NEW OLD STOCK.  This is a brand new part, never been attached to rubber or metal in any form.  For somebody doing a restoration, this is priceless.  Just wait, in ten years this will be worth 10 times that!  Go down to your local dealership and ask them how much this wheel is new from THEM...then tell me who's charging too much!<P>My grandfather said, "Something is worth what one man will give and what another man will take."  I'm a firm believer in that; if he wants fifty bucks and somebody will give it, that's what it's worth.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT<BR>||||reg||1
